# Build context is the repo root (backend/Dockerfile COPYs backend/*.py and
# frontend/). Keep everything the image does not need OUT of the context.
#
# Tests: `COPY backend/*.py .` matched every test_*.py and shipped the whole
# suite into the production image. Harmless while every fixture is synthetic,
# but the verbatim-fixture pattern was the root cause of every Phase 1 PII
# finding, so this is what would have DEPLOYED the next one. The build scripts
# run pytest from the working tree in Step 0, not inside the image, so nothing
# needs the tests in the context. (security review 2026-09-06)
backend/test_*.py
backend/__pycache__/
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/migration_validation/

# Local-only, gitignored, and secret-bearing. Never COPY'd, but never in the
# context either.
deploy.env
terraform/**/terraform.tfvars
research/
experiments/
.git/

# Claude Code session data, and any git worktree created under it. Nothing here
# can reach the IMAGE -- the Dockerfile's only COPY lines are
# backend/requirements.txt, backend/*.py and frontend/ -- and builds are local
# `docker build`, so the context never leaves the machine today. This is the
# guard for the day that changes: `gcloud builds submit` uploads the whole
# context to GCS, and a worktree under .claude/ can hold a symlinked corpus of
# real call-out forms (CLAUDE.md Rule #16 tells you to put worktrees OUTSIDE
# the repo for a related reason -- this covers the times that is forgotten).
.claude/
